@rossgee1091
You're really good at channeling the average Musk-cult member by blaring the "Yeah but there's a hidden backup in an inconvenient place, this totally justifies Tesla breaking what was working in the past" like that.

Well done, you really captured the essence of why argueing with Tesla fans is a bit like telling a brick wall to move: Even if it should, even if you'll demolish it when it won't, it's just never going to listen. I can only hope your channeling of other nutjob groups is as good.

@wemakecookie I agree people should not immediately judge because some car journalist can't get used to the new system within a few minutes.  I like many of the things Tesla does, but I am a big fan of haptic feedback, especially while driving. Stalks provide more feedback than buttons and buttons provide more feedback than a touchscreen, which essentially does not give any feedback at all, except that you touched it somewhere, hopefully where the button is located that you wanted to press. 

EV's are all about charging speed and not even so much about range. Bjorn Nyland has done some interesting videos with 1000km challenges and EV's and one of the best cars for many years remained the Hyundai Ionic Electric, because it could already charge at 75kW and hence beat many of the slower charging EV's with longer range. So long as 1000km on e single charge is not possible, his tests include fast charging and it is very easy to see that slow charging cars with decent range are not faster at their destination than quick charging cars with a shorter range. 

For that reason I would pick the Model 3, but I hear such mixed experiences with their reliability and Elon is a weird guy who does not seem to care about his customers at all. There is barely a dealer network to speak of in my country. I would have to drive for over an hour (55miles/87km) to get to the nearest one. My current car dealer is only a 15 minutes drive away (6 miles/10km). That is one of the advantages of the existing car manufacturers: they already have a huge service network. And I am sure BYD's situation will be even worse!

